#!/bin/bash
# A colleague runs this when nothing is open (merged, worktree removed, tasks
# handed over): the status bar and the team table show READY TO CLEAR. The mark
# is per sessionId, so after /clear (a new session) it goes away on its own.
pid=$$
while [ -n "$pid" ] && [ "$pid" -gt 1 ]; do
  [ -f "$HOME/.claude/sessions/$pid.json" ] && break
  pid=$(ps -o ppid= -p "$pid" | tr -d ' ')
done
sid=$(jq -r '.sessionId // empty' "$HOME/.claude/sessions/$pid.json" 2>/dev/null)
[ -z "$sid" ] && { echo "Could not find my Claude session." >&2; exit 1; }
mkdir -p "$HOME/.claude/tuned-clear"
touch "$HOME/.claude/tuned-clear/$sid"
echo "READY TO CLEAR set ($(jq -r '.name' "$HOME/.claude/sessions/$pid.json"))."
